<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Deploy-drift self-doctor.

    Runs deploy_drift_doctor.py hourly and answers one question nothing else in
    the fleet asks: is the running process running the code that was merged?

    Detects two distinct conditions, kept separate because their fixes differ:
      behind_origin   — merged commits the live checkout never pulled
                        (live-from-checkout surfaces only; the pinned deploy
                        worktree lags origin by design)
      restart_pending — checkout HEAD newer than the running process, i.e.
                        bytes on disk but the old module still in memory

    THIS DOCTOR NEVER HEALS. Pulling a live checkout and restarting
    governance-mcp is a production deploy on Lumen's check-in path, which is in
    the never-automate category (see memory: self-healing-doctor-layer,
    contract item 2). It diagnoses, escalates a fingerprinted finding, and
    closes that finding when the drift clears.

    Motivating incident (2026-07-28): unitares-pi-plugin #8 — Steward's missing
    core.agent_state write — merged with green CI and then sat dark in
    production for a day because the live checkout was never pulled. Found by a
    human asking "merged?", not by any detector.

    Before installing, substitute the placeholder:
      __UNITARES_ROOT__ -> absolute path to the deploy checkout
                           (e.g. $HOME/projects/unitares-deploy)

    Example:
      mkdir -p "$HOME/projects/unitares-deploy/data/logs"
      sed -e "s|__UNITARES_ROOT__|$HOME/projects/unitares-deploy|g" \
          scripts/ops/com.unitares.deploy-drift-doctor.plist.template \
          > ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.unitares.deploy-drift-doctor.plist
      launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.unitares.deploy-drift-doctor.plist

    Optional env:
      DEPLOY_DRIFT_DOCTOR_UUID       baselined governance identity; without it
                                     resolutions close locally but emit no
                                     outcome_event (an outcome row carrying no
                                     EISV would add noise to the label-breadth
                                     problem it is meant to help)
      DEPLOY_DRIFT_COOLDOWN_SECONDS  re-alert window per surface+condition
                                     (default 43200 = 12h)
-->
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN"
  "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key><string>com.unitares.deploy-drift-doctor</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/usr/bin/env</string>
        <string>python3</string>
        <string>__UNITARES_ROOT__/scripts/ops/deploy_drift_doctor.py</string>
    </array>
    <key>WorkingDirectory</key><string>__UNITARES_ROOT__</string>
    <key>StartInterval</key><integer>3600</integer>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>
    <key>ProcessType</key><string>Background</string>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>__UNITARES_ROOT__/data/logs/deploy-drift-doctor.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>__UNITARES_ROOT__/data/logs/deploy-drift-doctor.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
